---
description: Block non-English (Cyrillic) prose in docs/adr/ and backlog/tasks/
globs: ["docs/adr/**", "backlog/tasks/**"]
---

Do not introduce Cyrillic script into `docs/adr/*.md` or `backlog/tasks/*.md`.

The repo gate that enforces this is:
- `platform/tools/cyrillic/docs-adr-cyrillic-lint.mjs`
- `platform/.git/hooks/pre-commit`

It runs against staged files and flags any non-English prose outside code fences in
`platform/docs/` and `platform/backlog/` markdown.

Allowed exceptions:
- The small set of Ukrainian structural lines used by the ADR template in `docs/adr/`
  (for example `## Status`, `## Context`, `## Decision`, `## Consequences`, `## References`).
- Entire documents or doc sections that are deliberately authored in Ukrainian.

Not allowed:
- Cyrillic body prose, headings, tables, quotes, task metadata, or inline notes added to
  `docs/adr/` or `backlog/tasks/` outside code fences.
- Cyrillic inside the same-file markdown even if it looks “brief”; keep it in a code span,
  a quote with an English gloss, or translate it.

Quick check before staging:
- `node platform/tools/cyrillic/docs-adr-cyrillic-lint.mjs` should pass for the staged set.
- If you think a Cyrillic match is intentional, confirm whether it is the ADR structural
  baseline or the whole document is Ukrainian; otherwise translate the line.

Ancillary files that are not part of the docs/backlog markdown narrative (specimens,
screenshots, legal PDFs, backups) are out of scope for this rule.
